    "problem_statement": "Add a new capability to the RISC-V PMP stack-guard test that runs with CONFIG_PMP_NO_LOCK_GLOBAL=y, which omits the Lock bit from the global PMP entries so that the global PMP entries (null-pointer, ROM and stack-guard regions) can be reconfigured at boot. When this configuration option is enabled the PMP entries are left unlocked rather than permanently locked. With the option enabled, the stack guard region must still deny access so a write to it faults.",
